{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1113501-daywalking","id":1113501,"title":"Daywalking","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-08T19:38:32-07:00","id":1113501,"title":"Daywalking","content":"So I've been debating removing the sunlight bane, or at least altering it sufficiently that Kindred can survive in it.<br /> <br /> Humanity should limit rolls during the day, although I hesitate to limit die rolls to humanity dice. Maybe a penalty based on humanity? In some cases that could be harsher, as dice pools smaller than one's humanity could be reduced. It'd be less of a limitation for stronger Kindred, though.<br /> <br /> I am thinking 0 or 1 vitae per turn for all BP, or perhaps scaling like 1 vitae for 1-7, 2 for 8-9, and 3 for 0. Or some other scaling that is still restrictive even for the most powerful.<br /> <br /> For Disciplines, I am again thinking of 0 or 1 dot limits for everyone, or maybe allowing it to scale similarly to vitae above. So powerful elders will have a few additional tricks.<br /> <br /> Also, considering keeping things so that higher BP is penalized more than low BP by daytime.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure I am actually going to do this, but it's been on my mind as a possibility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T20:09:01-07:00","id":1113509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1113501-daywalking#post1113501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I've been debating removing the sunlight bane, or at least altering it sufficiently that Kindred can survive in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>What purpose would this serve?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T20:17:29-07:00","id":1113510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1113501-daywalking?p=1113509#post1113509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What purpose would this serve?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So the vamps sparkle in the sunlight???<br /> <br /> Anyway, a more serious thought is &quot;because crossover chronicle!&quot; Being stuck with a nocturnal cycle cramps their style around mages and, well, just about everyone except Forsaken werewolves (who like hunting under the moon very much, thank you).<br /> <br /> VtR 2.0 vamps already suffer very little damage at high humanity and low BP from sunlight. Low enough that they can afford to dash between cover or even go outside for a bit in a hoodie and not burst into flames. I'm not sure you need to do much more, frankly, but if greater activity is needed you don't have to dismiss the sunlight vulnerability that is core to the vampire myth--just dispense with some or all of the forced daysleep. Maybe impose a condition on operations during the day and make sleeping voluntary or based on a roll penalized by BP.<br /> <br /> That way, again, the higher BP the more it forces you toward traditional interactions with the sun. (Bursting into flames, screaming....)<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T20:30:07-07:00","id":1113513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1113501-daywalking?p=1113509#post1113509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What purpose would this serve?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would serve having vampires active during daytime, with some harsh (well, harsh for older more powerful vampires) restrictions. Let's just say I am debating if I want vampires active during the day and able to walk in the sun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1113501-daywalking?p=1113510#post1113510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the vamps sparkle in the sunlight???<br /> <br /> Anyway, a more serious thought is &quot;because crossover chronicle!&quot; Being stuck with a nocturnal cycle cramps their style around mages and, well, just about everyone except Forsaken werewolves (who like hunting under the moon very much, thank you).<br /> <br /> VtR 2.0 vamps already suffer very little damage at high humanity and low BP from sunlight. Low enough that they can afford to dash between cover or even go outside for a bit in a hoodie and not burst into flames. I'm not sure you need to do much more, frankly, but if greater activity is needed you don't have to dismiss the sunlight vulnerability that is core to the vampire myth--just dispense with some or all of the forced daysleep. Maybe impose a condition on operations during the day and make sleeping voluntary or based on a roll penalized by BP.<br /> <br /> That way, again, the higher BP the more it forces you toward traditional interactions with the sun. (Bursting into flames, screaming....)<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>Sunlight vulnerability is not core to the vampire myth, not before the past 95 years or so at any rate. The first vampire to burn in the sun was Count Orlok in the silent film <b>Nosferatu</b> released in 1922.<br /> <br /> The iconic vampire story, <b>Dracula</b>, features Dracula himself walking in daylight but deprived of his powers during daylight hours. &lt;-- This right here is what I'm thinking of doing. That's what the mechanics I described in my post were aimed at replicating, although I am thinking of allowing minimal power rather than none at all.<br /> <br /> Anyway, if I wanted to ponder the value of sticking with &quot;vampires burning in sunlight&quot; I wouldn't need to start a thread, so let's take it as read that such suggestions are not going to be taken and can we discuss ways to alter the rules so that daywalking is possible, but has harsh penalties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T20:37:55-07:00","id":1113521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1113501-daywalking?p=1113510#post1113510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, a more serious thought is &quot;because crossover chronicle!&quot; Being stuck with a nocturnal cycle cramps their style around mages and, well, just about everyone except Forsaken werewolves (who like hunting under the moon very much, thank you).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. But the 'why you want it' is really going to influence your mechanics, which is why I asked.<br /> <br /> If it's just wanting players to be more active you could switch out the penalties and change it to a Condition that affects them, the Condition giving them Beats when they play it up or causes them to suffer a setback.<br /> <br /> Because there's nothing fun about a flat 'stat decrease' mechanic, and if you want the players to play together they're all going to have to stay the same Humanity, which is an unreasonable limitation in most games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T20:39:46-07:00","id":1113522,"title":"","content":"Doesn't Resilience allow you to tank sunlight if it's high enough level? And it's a fairly easy discipline to learn.<br /> <br /> <br /> The problem isn't enduring the sunlight, it's staying awake during the daylight hours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T20:45:26-07:00","id":1113527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1113501-daywalking?p=1113521#post1113521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes. But the 'why you want it' is really going to influence your mechanics, which is why I asked.<br /> <br /> If it's just wanting players to be more active you could switch out the penalties and change it to a Condition that affects them, the Condition giving them Beats when they play it up or causes them to suffer a setback.<br /> <br /> Because there's nothing fun about a flat 'stat decrease' mechanic, and if you want the players to play together they're all going to have to stay the same Humanity, which is an unreasonable limitation in most games.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want vampires to be able to be active during daylight hours, and able to survive being in the sun for any length of time.<br /> <br /> Good point about the Beats, although I do want their ability to spend blood and use disciplines limited.<br /> <br /> What I described in the first post doesn't really mandate that everyone have the same humanity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1113501-daywalking?p=1113522#post1113522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't Resilience allow you to tank sunlight if it's high enough level? And it's a fairly easy discipline to learn.<br /> <br /> The problem isn't enduring the sunlight, it's staying awake during the daylight hours.</div> </div> </div> </div>Staying awake wouldn't be a problem with what I have in mind, and vampires won't need Resilience to survive sunlight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T21:03:55-07:00","id":1113543,"title":"","content":"Come to think of it, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> has more of a point than I understood on first reading.<br /> <br /> I'm gonna let this stuff go and see if I can come up with a condition that'll do what I want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T21:09:40-07:00","id":1113547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1113501-daywalking?p=1113527#post1113527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I want vampires to be able to be active during daylight hours, and able to survive being in the sun for any length of time.<br /> <br /> Good point about the Beats, although I do want their ability to spend blood and use disciplines limited.<br /> <br /> What I described in the first post doesn't really mandate that everyone have the same humanity.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Staying awake wouldn't be a problem with what I have in mind, and vampires won't need Resilience to survive sunlight.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well, some myths say that vampires can survive exposure to sunlight, but as long as they're in it, they lose access to their supernatural powers and are as vulnerable as humans. Such a weakness was originally present in Dracula, before he was later retconned to be killed by sunlight.<br /> <br /> Might I suggest you try out this approach?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T21:15:13-07:00","id":1113552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1113501-daywalking?p=1113547#post1113547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Well, some myths say that vampires can survive exposure to sunlight, but as long as they're in it, they lose access to their supernatural powers and are as vulnerable as humans. Such a weakness was originally present in Dracula, before he was later retconned to be killed by sunlight.<br /> <br /> Might I suggest you try out this approach?</div> </div> </div> </div>Check out the post that started this thread? That's the approach I was going with, although not necessarily &quot;as vulnerable as humans.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T21:23:21-07:00","id":1113556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1113501-daywalking?p=1113552#post1113552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Check out the post that started this thread? That's the approach I was going with, although not necessarily &quot;as vulnerable as humans.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Ah, I see. Well if that's the case, then it would be a viable option. The players could still interact with society, but they'd have to be extra careful about starting trouble, since they're effectively powerless until nightfall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T21:36:30-07:00","id":1113568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1113501-daywalking?p=1113556#post1113556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Ah, I see. Well if that's the case, then it would be a viable option. The players could still interact with society, but they'd have to be extra careful about starting trouble, since they're effectively powerless until nightfall.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed.<br /> <br /> I'm going to redo things as a condition that can earn beats and see how that looks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T23:48:35-07:00","id":1113627,"title":"","content":"If the problem is 'staying awake' not 'bursting into flames' - May I suggest idea of locking out 1 Willpower point for day activities and Humanity dice pools limits? <br /> <br /> It would work like this - beside possibility of catching the flame, Willpower 5 character will have to use ma 4 WP to be spent in the Day ( with 1 WP constanty used on staying awake) - and when he does, he will go to Torpor, to get at least 1 WP at dysk and night. It force vampires to be MUCH more alerted in Day ( by making it more harder to stay awake) but it's also no deal breaking - and high Willpower vampires can easily mang\u0119 it. ( As it should be, my I add).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-09-2017, 02:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T00:55:14-07:00","id":1113642,"title":"","content":"Isn't sunlight considerably less harmful the lower your blood potency and higher your humanity is in 2e? Something like just created vampires taking 1 bashing every 4 or so hours if I recall correctly. Or is this hack supposed to be for 1e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T01:10:35-07:00","id":1113644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1113501-daywalking?p=1113642#post1113642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't sunlight considerably less harmful the lower your blood potency and higher your humanity is in 2e? Something like just created vampires taking 1 bashing every 4 or so hours if I recall correctly. Or is this hack supposed to be for 1e?</div> </div> </div> </div>True of 2e as well. But it's lethal damage minimum, even with 7-10 Humanity.<br /> <br /> Specifically: 1 lethal at Humanity 7-10, 2L at Humanity 6, 3L at Humanity 5, 1A at Humanity 4, and increases until you get 5A at Humanity 0.<br /> Meanwhile, Blood Potency 1-2 gives you a ten-minute interval. BP 3 gives you one minute, and BP 4-5 gives you a turn. At BP 6-7 a single turn counts as two intervals, at BP 8-9 a single turn is three intervals, and finally at BP 10 a single turn is five intervals.<br /> <br /> So a Humanity 10, BP 1 vampire would suffer one level of lethal damage every 10 minutes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":".  typo 07-09-2017, 04:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T02:19:07-07:00","id":1113661,"title":"","content":"If you're completely covered, like gloves, full clothes and a hood with the head tilted down you dont suffer any damage if you're BP1. <br /> And you could interpret the table as intervals that must be filled. Like every ten minutes, 0-9 minutes is still not ten. So a BP1 vampire could walk around the day walking between shadows, taking a bit precaution and cover and you'll be fine. Cloudy and rainy days dont have much daylight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T09:43:34-07:00","id":1113776,"title":"","content":"This thread really isn't for discussing how to use the existing rules, but rather to use new rules that don't involve damage from sunlight and an ability to stay up during the day without the need for rolls or spending willpower or whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T10:30:37-07:00","id":1113786,"title":"","content":"So like daytime would impose a condition on Kindred that would limit their access to disciplines and ability to spend vitae. I'm still not sure where exactly I want to draw the line in each case, but I know these are both going to be a thing.<br /> <br /> What I've been thinking is that the condition resolves at sunset, but returns at sunrise. And every time it causes a serious problem you get a Beat. Like it's going to cause nuisance level issues all day, but in addition you'll have situations like being unable to heal because of vitae limits or a discipline might enable to resolve a situation but you can't use it.<br /> <br /> This is kind of vague, but it's basically where I'm at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T11:50:59-07:00","id":1113806,"title":"","content":"Do you think there could also be a bonus to resist frenzy during the day? Would that work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T11:51:55-07:00","id":1113807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1113501-daywalking?p=1113806#post1113806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think there could also be a bonus to resist frenzy during the day? Would that work?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting thought! It would make sense if the beast itself is sleepy during the day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T20:59:12-07:00","id":1114026,"title":"","content":"Ok, Ok. I'll admit to unnecessary flippancy and apologize. Actually the direction of conversation is interesting enough I may well have a struggle not to *try* the approach myself. There are some significant implications on vampire society and play that should be batted around.... but first, a contribution.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Daywalker</i> (Condition)</b><br /> You have succeeded in thwarting your beast and remained conscious under the eye of the sun while it is thrust into slumber. With it the curse sleeps, but that can be a drawback as well as a benefit. You may only spend vitae for Blush of Life and do not gain vitae from feeding; similarly your vitae is powerless to embrace childer or ghoul mortals. Persistent Discipline effects are reduced by 1 for each point of Blood Potency, and Discipline and Devotion activation rolls are penalized by 1 for each point of Blood Potency.<br /> <br /> Sunlight burns you more like an unfortunate sufferer of porphyria, and less like a supernatural scouring--reduce all damage a severity step (lethal to bashing, aggravated to lethal) and increase all times (minutes to hours, turns to minutes). Mundane sunlight protections are much more effective as well: full covering (only eyes revealed) reduces your effective Blood Potency for damage calculation by three levels, and a heavily overcast day by a further two levels; lesser covering may provide smaller reductions to effective Blood Potency. If your effective Blood Potency is reduced to zero for sunlight damage, no damage is suffered even under extended exposure.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Your sleeping Beast sullenly bothers you less: take a bonus of half your Humanity (rounded down) to resist frenzy. However it also aids you less in resisting supernatural effects or projecting your own nature: halve your Blood Potency (rounded down) for purposes of Lashing Out or resisting in a Clash of Wills.</span></span><br /> <br /> When <i>Daywalker</i> resolves, impose the <i>Tempted</i> condition, as your Beast remains none too happy with your shenanigans.<br /> <br /> <u>Possible Sources:</u> Spending a Willpower point and succeeding in a Willpower contest with successes equal to your Blood Potency, to remain awake at dawn.<br /> <br /> <u>Resolution:</u> Nightfall.<br /> <br /> <u>Beat:</u> Take a beat if your weakened condition puts you in danger of destruction or breach of the Masquerade, requiring more elaborate measures than your supernatural powers would usually provide for.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit and amend!<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12493,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","user":"Khanwulf","date":"blue). 07-10-2017, 11:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T21:30:52-07:00","id":1114038,"title":"","content":"That is an excellent starting point, and has me thinking about possibilities of keeping some degree of sun burnination. Thanks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I mean I want staying awake to be easier at the very least, but this is a nice compromise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 07-10-2017, 12:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T04:06:52-07:00","id":1114102,"title":"","content":"What you could do is pillage (some of) the mechanics of the Coil of the Ascendant and just give them to all vampires for free.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T08:30:59-07:00","id":1114167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1113501-daywalking?p=1114038#post1114038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is an excellent starting point, and has me thinking about possibilities of keeping some degree of sun burnination. Thanks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I mean I want staying awake to be easier at the very least, but this is a nice compromise.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, emphasis on starting point. For example, I forgot to include a bonus to resist frenzy--which could be up to Humanity/2? Also, what effect on BP for Clash of Wills purposes? (Important when resisting other supernaturals/ephemerals).<br /> <br /> Add:<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Your sleeping Beast sullenly bothers you less: take a bonus of half your Humanity (rounded down) to resist frenzy. However it also aids you less in resisting supernatural effects or projecting your own nature: halve your Blood Potency (rounded down) for purposes of Lashing Out or resisting in a Clash of Wills.</span></span><br /> <br /> I think the thread deserves some practical thinking on the in-game repercussions of vampires being able to choose to set aside most of their supernatural ability and walk in daylight (at least when at low BP--and Dracula had recently arisen from torpor, no?). Starting with the above:<br /> <br /> 1. You cannot heal during the day.<br /> 2. You cannot feed, which means daytime is mostly useless for hunting unless you're into kidnapping for a larder.<br /> 3. Your physical disciplines *may* still provide a benefit, if they are higher than your BP.<br /> 4. Your non-physical disciplines are mostly useless, the exceptions being Animalism 1, Auspex 1, 2 (first uses) and 3; Dominate 1, 3 and sometimes 2; Majesty 1 and 2; Nightmare 1; Obfuscate 1; Protean 1 (soil only); and a few Devotions that do not require vitae (and that I don't care to research). Even those that you can attempt, you are at a significant penalty to, depending on BP.<br /> 5. You start the day down at least one Willpower point--possibly more if your BP is edging up there and you had to spend for more dice on the roll. --You are tired, in other words!<br /> 6. Your defenses are severely degraded: any mortal is a threat and can at least put you into torpor. Since the condition wears off at nightfall regardless of your state, being left in a field means you'll start smoking tomorrow, anyway.<br /> 7. Frenzy is going to be a potential issue in the evening. This worsens for repeated Daywalking, if meaningful interaction with Touchstones is not feasible. (There may be other conditions that should be applied, more than just <i>Tempted.</i>)<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that you are thereby actually *Weaker* than Ghouls under this condition, as written!<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what the Lancea would think of their flock setting aside the curse to walk in day, but if it's just a thing some vampires *can* do, probably they'd look at it as an opportunity to further the Kindred mandate for harassing mortals. Or something. Someone can do Sanctum better than I.<br /> <br /> Benefits?<br /> <br /> 1. You can see the sun without your eyeballs running like wax. That's a thing.<br /> 2. Significantly easier interaction with Touchstones.<br /> 3. Ghouls no longer absolutely necessary to stand in line for you at the local license branch. (For example.) Avoiding this codependency plot is a significant twist from base VtR, and makes ghouls more of a voluntary matter or something you slide into needing as BP increases.<br /> 4. As you rise in BP, your alien-ness and estrangement from the day increases. This slow degradation serves as a second note to the sudden loss of the day at embrace.<br /> 5. Instead of being the All Night Society you have vampires embedded like ticks in mortal society much more deeply. That weird guy at the library all day? Your office colleague who always has a half-full coffee cup you never see him drink? The woman in the power heels at the municipal department building who no one knows her job? The guy in a beater hoodie hanging with the homeless all the time at the park even when it's 90 out? Heck--that shaggy, wolf-like dog in the neighborhood who lives in the culvert? Your high-school classmate who vanished over the summer two years ago and now makes straight-As despite all-night band sessions? Absolutely anyone and everyone 9-5 could be a vampire waiting to shed their mortal skin--figuratively, of course. Note: being a modern vampire is rather easier than during ages before electric lights, when people just went to bed as the sun went down.<br /> 6. Much more personal time as a vampire--more similar to mortals, in fact, who can choose to push themselves over a week or so to get more done (reading, study, other activity) but have to crash eventually. As a vampire your willpower WILL go out if you pursue frequent daywalking, leaving you more vulnerable at night when the real horrors are out. Keep in mind that vampires do not, RAW, receive a Willpower point per day, and if they're up all day then they wouldn't have a &quot;waking&quot; moment at nightfall anyway (though they should spend a vitae point per normal as the sun sets).<br /> 7. Hanging out with other cross-splat supernaturals now a LOT easier to justify and arrange: werewolves? Sure, be a pack member! Mages? A valuable research assistant and backup muscle. All the others? You're now relevant as opposed to being a literal boat-anchor half of every 24-hour cycle. This in fact makes a time-skipping cross-splat chronicle more viable as well, as the vampire can serve as a narrative anchor as others age and die around her. (I'm reminded of the first, Promethean, fiction in Tales of the Dark Eras.)<br /> <br /> Another note to this essay: you won't have BP 4 or 5 vampires pursuing any kind of Daywalking lifestyle for long. Either they burn out their Willpower pool in a couple of nights, or they end up failing a roll and missing planned activities. That means either Torpor becomes a thing, or you see a LOT more XP dumped into upping Willpower. Keep in mind Willpower has no bound, so a truly dedicated Daywalker could accumulate 20 or 30 dice to throw at the problem of consistency in the face of rising BP. Most won't do that however, and slide inevitably into the slow horror of the night.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12493,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","user":"Khanwulf","date":".  Extra condition text. 07-10-2017, 11:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T10:41:29-07:00","id":1114205,"title":"","content":"<di